{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Finiteness"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.surjective_algebraMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.surjective_algebraMap","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.lean#L102-L112","doc":"Consequence: every element of `A` lies in the image of `algebraMap R A`.\nSo `A` is a quotient of `R`, i.e. at most one-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.eq_counit_smul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.eq_counit_smul_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.lean#L69-L100","doc":"**Collapse.** A multiplicative counit on a Frobenius algebra forces\n`x = ε(x) • 1` for every `x`. No antipode is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.contract_mul_one_tmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.contract_mul_one_tmul","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.lean#L55-L67","doc":"The counit-law contraction `rid ∘ lTensor ε` applied to `comul 1 * (1 ⊗ₜ x)`,\nwhen `comul 1 = Σᵢ aᵢ ⊗ₜ bᵢ`, is `Σᵢ ε(bᵢ x) • aᵢ`. Proved by induction on\nthe tensor `t = comul 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}